            "Friendship needs time, repetition, shared experience, and enough freedom for kids to build their own bonds. It cannot be solved with one-off activities or parent networking alone.",
            "A serious alternative to school has to design for that. Teams, clubs, gyms, neighborhoods, cousins, church if relevant, volunteer groups, classes, jobs, and recurring local structures matter because they create repeated contact instead of isolated enrichment events."
