            "You do it deliberately, because default school attendance will not be doing it for you. The family needs recurring places where the child is known, expected, useful, and missed when absent.",
            "The key word is recurring. A museum day is nice, but it is not community by itself. A team, class, gym, job, volunteer shift, neighborhood routine, maker group, or family network that repeats over time can become real social ground."
