            "Temperament deserves respect. A shy child does not need to be turned into a performer, and an awkward child does not need to be shamed into polish. But temperament is not a full exemption from social capability.",
            "The target is functional confidence: asking for help, joining a group, handling basic conversation, repairing mistakes, and building a few real relationships. That can be taught gently and seriously without pretending every child should become socially flashy."
